  "verbalization": "Notoamide B appears to have a shared target of H9 across three distinct pathways, with varying levels of confidence in the evidence. The first pathway links Notoamide B to Malme-3M, which is targeted by Linustatin, and then to H9. The second pathway connects Notoamide B to Malme-3M, which is targeted by Methyl 4-Formylbenzoate, and then to H9. The third pathway links Notoamide B to A498, which is targeted by Caragasinin B, and then to H9. These findings suggest that Notoamide B may act through a common mechanism to inhibit H9, potentially by targeting a shared downstream pathway or a common cellular process.\n\nThe evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of Notoamide B acting as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately inhibit H9. The high scores in all three paths indicate a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets (Malme-3M, A498) suggests that Notoamide B may interact with different cellular processes, possibly through distinct pathways that converge on H9. The integration of these pathways implies that Notoamide B may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, with H9 being a central node in this network. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Notoamide B and H9, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mode of action.",
